# Local env holds a LIVE provider credential — never commit it.
# (On the deployed host there is no such file: the key is a `pass://`
# pointer in the profile, resolved by the daemon. See template/.)
.env
!.env.example

# The project's own virtualenv (uv sync --extra tui) and its lock.
.venv/
uv.lock
__pycache__/

# NOTHING BELOW HERE SHOULD EXIST IN A CLEAN CHECKOUT.
#
# This repository is the implementation and the template; it is NOBODY'S
# WORKSPACE (see workspace.py).  A session runs in
# `<root>/<caller>/workspace`, so memories, references, documents,
# recordings and session journals belong THERE and never here.
#
# These entries remain for two reasons: this checkout still holds the
# store from before that separation, and a `--workspace .` run would put
# more of it here.  They are a safety net against committing somebody's
# second brain, not a description of the layout.
.jaato/
docs/
audio/

# The template is COPIED INTO workspaces, so runtime state must never
# accumulate in it: whatever is here is laid down in the next person's
# workspace.  `workspace.py` skips these on copy as well — belt and
# braces, because one leak is one person reading another's memories.
template/.jaato/memory/
template/.jaato/references/
template/.jaato/sessions/
template/.jaato/logs/
template/.jaato/forgotten/
template/.jaato/.artifact_tracker.json
template/.jaato/discarded_references.json
template/docs/
template/audio/
template/.env
